{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cd9fba59b6ee1db3adebb3cdfacd4415b94500f63036fd81387e534e1f6e1c2f","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM failure handling and operator messaging","key_entities":["message_for()","RESOLUTION_MESSAGES","ResolutionClass.CHANGE_INPUT","CONTENT_FILTER_MESSAGE","finish_reason","LLMOutcome.diagnostic","src/rebar/llm/failure.py","src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","stopReason=guardrail_intervened"],"problem_keywords":["content filter","guardrail","misleading message","operator messaging","resolution message","finish reason","content policy"],"propositions":["When an LLM call is blocked by a content policy (Bedrock Guardrail or Anthropic refusal), the operator-facing message incorrectly reports 'too large / malformed' instead of naming the real cause.","The message_for() function must be enhanced to accept an optional finish_reason parameter and return a distinct message when resolution_class is CHANGE_INPUT and finish_reason is 'content_filter'.","Non-content-filter CHANGE_INPUT cases (HTTP 413, context-length 400) must continue returning the existing generic message.","The resolution_class, retryable flag, and exit-code behavior remain unchanged; only the operator-facing message text is refined."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787890619856109001,"uuid":"edb19ad3-6465-47b7-b620-f550c381d008"}